                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Oh...Sir! Is like a fighting game, but rather than fists, feet, and projectile spamming, words are your weapons. You can play online with friends and randos, or with your friends and family at home. There are also single player modes, including a tournament mode. Tournament mode is where you will unlock most of the hidden characters and stages. We'll touch up on this later.\n\nNow, for gameplay, you and the other player/COM player pick a character. You then take turns clicking on words to make an insult. You must start with a subject (Your mother, You, Your math teacher) and follow with a verb (never watched Star Wars, Farts in your general direction, is/are ugly etc). Conjunctions like And can help you stretch your insult as far as you can. If you try to use something that doesn't work or follow something you said, you take damage. Each player also has their teacup. You get two additional words that the other player cannot access. And if you use them, or they don't help you, drink your tea to refresh the word bank. These can often come in clutch and turn the tides. In online play, you can't see your opponents' extra words and vice versa. T\n\nEach character has a specific weakness. For example, Sir Arthur Knight does not have an understanding of modern technology. Therefore, if you throw things like \"Never Watched Star Wars\" or \"Still uses Windows Vista\" at him, it will do extra damage. Sir Arthur Knight can still use these words, but they won't deal that extra damage to anyone who is not himself. In that instance it's more of a defensive play, taking the weakness away from your opponent so they can't use it against you. \n\nUsing combos (using the same words across multiple insults), weaknesses, and stretching that insult out as far as you can, you can shave huge portions of damage off the opponent. Out of words? Don't have anything that works? Then you can click on the (...) button and this will let you postpone your insult. However, it can backfire and kill your insult if your opponent's insult is particularly stinging. So it's a risk vs reward kind of thing.\n\nThere are five settings and each setting even includes extra words that are exclusive to that stage. The pet shop, for example, throws in words like \"Belongs in one of those cages.\" And \"Every one of those animals\" that do not appear in any other stage.\n\nGoing back to tournament mode, it is a five round single player campaign. The five levels are set in stone, but the opponent is randomized (barring the final stage) You'll need to play through it multiple times to unlock the hidden characters, but the nice part of that is if you lose or quit, you just return to the stage you were on, and there doesn't appear to be any penalty for losing. Tournament mode only takes about 30-45 minutes to complete, but the added ability to return later is nice. You still have to start that stage over but I will take that over having to redo the whole mode again.",
